  "tier": "told-once",
  "plain": "The idea is that in 1947, near Roswell, New Mexico, the site of a famous crash that year, two craft were flying low and close together in a lightning storm, scanning for plutonium, the material in nuclear bombs. One craft measured the background noise and the other picked up the signal. Dr. John Brandenburg, a guest who argues that life on Mars was wiped out by nuclear war, puts this forward as his own theory, crediting a book called Cosmic Awakening, as a way to explain why craft would be over the area at all."
